&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe, LLC. is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies - from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups - use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone&#39;s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Architect, build, and maintain robust APIs, services, and systems across engineering teams using Ruby and Java;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Act as a domain expert of the payments family of Stripe products, and in particular various payout methods and underlying rails used in US / UK;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and enhance software infrastructure, encompassing the complete development lifecycle from coding to testing, deployment, debugging, and maintenance;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design software systems leveraging scientific analysis and mathematical models to predict and measure design outcomes;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to core interface design and write code;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as a role model for how great software should be written;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute code changes in every layer of the stack, from launching a net new payout method API to making a UI change in the Stripe Dashboard for the Stripe Connect product; Scope and lead technical projects, laying the groundwork for early-stage products to iteratively evolve and scale;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Engineer payments integration with banking partners to launch new markets, payout methods, and capabilities, while ensuring reliability and scalability;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with engineers across the company to build new features at large-scale;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design and implement secure systems for sensitive data storage;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with engineers across the company to understand when existing infrastructure can be leveraged vs. when building a bespoke solution is necessary;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Evaluate and make informed decisions about technology and architecture choices in developing payment products;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and execute short- and long-term roadmaps, making informed trade-offs to balance business priorities, user experience, and a sustainable technical foundation;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure technical decisions align with broader strategic goals while addressing specific emerging business needs;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and direct software system testing and validation procedures, programming, and documentation to ensure reliability; and&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Participate in the 24/7 on-call rota to manage and resolve production incidents affecting users.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Bachelor&#39;s degree or foreign equivalent in Computer Science or a related field followed by 2 years of experience in Software Development.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Position also requires 2 years of experience with the following:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Building software solutions in Python, Ruby, Java and Typescript languages;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Designing, building and working with large user-facing APIs;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Translating business needs into software requirements and designs;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Debugging production issues across services and multiple levels of the stack;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Designing, building, and maintaining scalable, high availability systems; and&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Designing and implementing secure systems for sensitive data storage.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Salary: $156,800 - $235,200/yr.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This salary range represents the base salary range for the role and any sales commissions/sales bonuses targets, if applicable, would be in addition to the base salary.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;40 hrs/week&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;50% Telecommuting permitted.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Multiple Positions Available.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Additional benefits for this role may include: equity, company bonus or sales commissions/bonuses; 401(k) plan; medical, dental, and vision benefits; and wellness stipends.&lt;strong&gt;CA47&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
